<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>DW - English for Africa</title><subtitle type="html">News, Analysis and Service from Germany and Europe - in 30 Languages</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-africa" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12756?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-africa" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Uber leaves two key African markets — and their drivers in despair</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:45cd5c9fc75c668f4aa68c73ca794b79bf4b77060b745efe420081a2f951095f</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T12:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189--bdbc88dc3498.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uber-leaves-two-key-african-markets-and-their-drivers-in-despair/a-79232189?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Uber's departure from Nigeria and Uganda has left countless customers high and dry. But what about drivers? With fuel prices, maintenance and other operating costs rising, many say they're struggling to make a living.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spanish lawmakers back citizenship for Sahrawis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f2c6378a46edafac8468159ae3f5f584aa7b4f2385c316f6359e3b806e548c99</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-11T03:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spanish-lawmakers-back-citizenship-for-sahrawis/a-79222841--98a92dd37696.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spanish-lawmakers-back-citizenship-for-sahrawis/a-79222841?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spanish lawmakers approved a bill that could give citizenship to tens of thousands of Sahrawis and their descendants, amid tense ties with Morocco. The legislation must now pass the senate.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Algeria cuts diplomatic ties with UAE</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53aea7f232080b24aab03ac8fd7a01fb978af6bb2ce0cf27e7a1a947c747bb68</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T22:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/algeria-cuts-diplomatic-ties-with-uae/a-79222141--9a0191878148.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/algeria-cuts-diplomatic-ties-with-uae/a-79222141?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Algeria said that it was closing its airspace and severing ties with the United Arab Emirates. Algiers accuses Abu Dhabi of destabilizing countries such as Libya, Sudan and Mali.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Uganda: Traditional kingdom plunged into succession crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:df736aa5df91eaef387982070d9a0a1e1a58ed182b52269dd6398785aff2e752</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-10T13:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uganda-traditional-kingdom-plunged-into-succession-crisis/a-79214786--f0980c6e478f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uganda-traditional-kingdom-plunged-into-succession-crisis/a-79214786?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A royal succession committee and the family of late King Oyo Nyimba of Toroo have put forward competing candidates. Questions have been raised as to whether the late monarch indeed had a son as his family claims.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>The billion-euro trade driving Europe's eels to extinction</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e172fe70f7153edb4ee378e1b9e62a24a57d1a1bb4aca7ae907f2d3220167dc4</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145--e574ad564b10.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-billion-euro-trade-driving-europe-s-eels-to-extinction/a-78523145?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Traffickers are making big bucks smuggling millions of critically endangered eels across continents, using suitcases on planes and legal loopholes to deliver them to dinnerplates. Where are the smuggling hotspots?</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Trafficked into fraud: An African crisis situation in Cambodia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:372e9691737e68a41488661b7518a4711aa0effb9f32de54573a802040f607c0</id><updated>2026-09-12T04:45:22Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T08:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967--d423991a2cca.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trafficked-into-fraud-an-african-crisis-situation-in-cambodia/a-79189967?maca=en-rss-en-africa-8291-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Cambodia's crackdown on scam operators is stranding young African trafficking victims in the Asian country with no money, no passport and no prospects.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
